GAL22V10
BERRWDOG

CDAC AS DTACK AB21 AB22 AB23 NC7 NC8 NC9 NC10 NC11 GND
NC13 Q0 Q1 Q2 Q3 Q4 Q5 Q6 Q7 NC22 BERR VCC

; =====================================================================
; BERR watchdog for RocHard $200000 RAM diagnostics
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; A no-DTACK access to the card's RAM window hangs the 68000 forever
; (stock A500 has no bus-error timeout for this space). This GAL asserts
; /BERR (68000 pin 22 / expansion pin 46) if _DTACK does not arrive
; within ~8 CDAC cycles (~2.2us) of an _AS-active access INSIDE the
; $200000-$3FFFFF window. The CPU then takes a bus-error exception
; instead of hanging, so a memtest can log the faulting address and
; continue.
;
; WINDOW-GATED: only arms for AB23=0,AB22=0,AB21=1 ($200000-$3FFFFF),
; so it never false-triggers on chip RAM / Kickstart / CIA cycles.
;
; enable = in-window & _AS asserted & _DTACK not-yet-asserted
;        = AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
;   (AS,DTACK are active-low: /AS = asserted, DTACK = not-acked/high.
;    ABx probed at U10 outputs = active-high: AB21=1 at $200000.)
;
; 8-stage shift register clocked by CDAC. When enable drops (DTACK
; arrives or cycle ends or address leaves window) the whole chain
; clears in one clock (each stage ANDs enable). Q7 => timeout => BERR.
;
; /BERR is DRIVEN LOW only during timeout, Hi-Z otherwise (wire-OR with
; the 68000's pull-up and any other BERR source).
;
; WIRING:
;   pin1  CDAC   <- J1.15
;   pin2  AS     <- J1.74 (_AS)
;   pin3  DTACK  <- J1.66 (_DTACK)
;   pin4  AB21   <- U10.13
;   pin5  AB22   <- U10.15
;   pin6  AB23   <- U10.17
;   pin23 BERR   -> expansion slot pin 46 (68000 /BERR)
;   pin12 GND, pin24 VCC
;
; TUNING: timeout = 8 CDAC (~2.2us) >> a valid RAM DTACK (~0.4us). If
; legit slow cycles false-trigger, add stages / slow the clock; if you
; want faster recovery, tap BERR off an earlier Qn.
; =====================================================================


; ---- 8-stage timeout shift register (registered, clk = CDAC) --------
Q0.R = AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q1.R = /Q0 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q2.R = /Q1 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q3.R = /Q2 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q4.R = /Q3 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q5.R = /Q4 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q6.R = /Q5 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK
Q7.R = /Q6 & AB21 & /AB22 & /AB23 & /AS & DTACK


; ---- /BERR (pin 23): drive LOW during timeout, else Hi-Z ------------
; BERR declared active-high (no slash). .T tautological-false -> data 0
; -> pin LOW when enabled. .E = Q7 -> only driven during timeout.
BERR.T = AS & /AS
BERR.E = /Q7


DESCRIPTION

BERR timeout watchdog for RocHard $200000 RAM diagnostics.

Asserts /BERR (expansion pin 46) if _DTACK is absent for ~8 CDAC cycles
during an _AS access in the $200000-$3FFFFF window, converting the
otherwise-fatal no-DTACK hang into a 68000 bus-error exception so a
memtest can log the faulting address and continue. Window-gated (never
fires outside the card RAM space); /BERR driven low only during timeout,
Hi-Z otherwise.
